{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mdj2rs3y6zgjgnrcxer7qx5jek6hyy7ckx22ebtar6quhq6oaifa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **All gates pass** — and one real translation bug was found and fixed.\n\n## The bug: NaN payload selection\n\n`cargo check` was clean and symbols already matched 28/28, but Phase B rows 2, 3 and 6 **failed**. The pre-existing module doc in `lib.rs` claimed this divergence was unfixable \"GCC algebraic rewriting.\" That was wrong.\n\nDisassembling the reference `.so` showed it's built at **`-O0`** — one instruction per source operator. On x86, when *both* operands of `ADDSS`/`MULSS` are NaN, the **destination** register's payload propagates, and GCC's `-O0` register allocation does not consistently put the left source operand there:\n\n| site | destination |\n|---|---|\n| `c2Add`: `a.x + b.x` | `b.x` (right) |\n| `c2Dot`: final `addss` | the *second* product |\n| `c2MulmvT`: both lanes' `addss` | the *second* product |\n| `c2RaytoAABB`: `tN * A.t` | `A.t` (right) |\n| `c2RaytoCapsule`: `yAp.y + (…)*t` | the *product* (right) |\n\nPlain Rust `+`/`*` lets LLVM commute freely, so it picked the other operand. Fixed by adding explicit `addss`/`subss`/`mulss`/`divss` helpers and pinning the operand order at each of ~30 arithmetic sites to what `objdump -d` actually emits. Every site now carries a comment recording the evidence.\n\n## Results\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `nm -D` symbol diff | **empty** (28/28, 0 missing, 0 extra, no non-libc undefined) |\n| Phase B — 50/50 `CONFIGS.md` rows | pass, **1,054,605 bit-exact comparisons** |\n| Phase C — 40/40 testable `ERRORS.md` rows | pass (42 tests) |\n| Configurations | no `[features]`, no `[[bin]]`; verified in **debug *and* release** |\n\nEverything goes through `libloading` on both `.so` files — never a direct Rust call — comparing raw `u32` bit patterns so `-0.0` and NaN payloads can't be glossed over.\n\nTwo things worth flagging beyond the checklist:\n\n- **Out-params start from a `dirty()` pattern, not zeros.** This surfaced that `c2RaytoCapsule` writes `out->n`/`out->t` *before* its `return 0` paths — a miss still mutates the caller's struct. Zero-filling would have hidden it.\n- **`err_08` (`hit == 0`) is unreachable without NaN.** Working through `c2RayToPlane_OneDimensional`, its result is provably `<= 1` for all finite inputs, so `t <= 1.0f` can only be false when `t` is NaN. My first random search never hit the branch; the test now injects NaN deliberately and reaches it 33 times. Coverage assertions elsewhere (all 4 AABB normals, all 4 poly faces, all 9 capsule branches via an oracle built from the C's own exports) guard against the same class of silent-pass.\n\n`./verify.sh` reruns the whole gate; `c_src/` untouched apart from the untracked `build/` dir. Note I added `.cargo/config.toml` with `offline = true` since the crates.io index is blocked here — `libloading 0.8.9` resolved from the local cache."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":218060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":570,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc8a2434-34fa-441c-b87b-6130e16867fd","uuid":"7dedb0f0-4372-4716-8d4f-14fa0a24da98","timestamp":"2026-09-05T10:48:29.991Z"}
